\begin{theorem}\label{thm:phase-transition}
Let $\cC$ be a block-stable class of connected graphs, let $\cB$ be its class of $2$-connected components whose EGF we denote by $B(y)$, and let $\rho_B$ be the radius of convergence of $B$. Let
\[u_C := \frac{1}{\rho_B B''(\rho_B)}.\]
Then the following hold. 
\begin{itemize}
    \item The singular behaviour of $C^{\bullet}(x,u)$ depends on the relative positions of $u$ and $u_C$;
