\begin{thm}[Kato \cite{Kato}, see also \cite{CL}, \cite{LLMS}]\label{thm:Kato}
There is an injective  homomorphism of $R(T)$-algebra 
$\Phi: K_*^T(\Gr_G)_\loc\rightarrow QK_T(G/B)_{\mathrm{loc}}$ such that
\begin{align}
\OGr_{t_\beta}&\mapsto Q^{\beta}\quad \text{for anti-dominant $\beta\in Q^\lor$,}\label{eq:Phi ell}
\\
\bO^w&\mapsto \CO^w\quad\text{for $w\in W$}.
\label{eq:Phi Q}
\end{align}
In particular, we have
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:Qk}
{\prod_{j\in I}\sigma_j^{-\langle \alpha_k^\lor,\alpha_j\rangle}}\mapsto Q_k\quad (k\in I).
\end{equation}
\end{thm}

ref_dict.thm:main:
\begin{thm}\label{thm:main}
Let $i$ be a special (cominuscule) node of the Dynkin diagram of $G,$
and $\miw{i}$ the Seidel element corresponding to $i$. Then,  for any $w\in W,$ we have 
    $$
\CO^{\miw{i}}\cdot \miw{i}^L{\CO^w}=Q^{\piv_i-w^{-1}(\piv_i)}\CO^{\miw{i} w}
$$
 in torus-equivatiant quantum $K$-theory $QK_T(G/B)$. 
\end{thm}

expanded_sketch:
Our proof relies on the ``quantum equals affine'' philosophy, which goes back to Peterson \cite{Pet}. A central ingredient is the $K$-theoretic Peterson isomorphism, conjectured in Ikeda--Lenart--Li--Maeno--Shimozono, and established by Kato. We use the following result.

\begin{thm}[Kato \cite{Kato}, see also \cite{CL}, \cite{LLMS}]\label{thm:Kato}
There is an injective  homomorphism of $R(T)$-algebra 
$\Phi: K_*^T(\Gr_G)_\loc\rightarrow QK_T(G/B)_{\mathrm{loc}}$ such that
\begin{align}
\OGr_{t_\beta}&\mapsto Q^{\beta}\quad \text{for anti-dominant $\beta\in Q^\lor$,}\label{eq:Phi ell}
\\
\bO^w&\mapsto \CO^w\quad\text{for $w\in W$}.
\label{eq:Phi Q}
\end{align}
In particular, we have
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:Qk}
{\prod_{j\in I}\sigma_j^{-\langle \alpha_k^\lor,\alpha_j\rangle}}\mapsto Q_k\quad (k\in I).
\end{equation}
\end{thm}

It yields an isomorphism of $R(T)$-algebras
\[
\Phi:
K_*^T(\Gr_G)_{\mathrm{loc}}\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } QK_T(G/B)_{\mathrm{loc}}.
\]
We also use an extended version of the $K$-theoretic nil-Hecke algebra developed by Ikeda--Shimozono--Yamaguchi \cite{ISY}: the commutative subalgebra $\ePet$ (the extended $K$-theoretic Peterson algebra) inside $\hat{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{af}}$, together with its natural action (incorporating the $\hat{W}_{\mathrm{af}}$-symmetry, in particular the action of $\Sigma\simeq \pi_1(G^{\mathrm{ad}})$).

(Additionally, the parabolic Corollary~\ref{cor:P} is said to follow immediately in establishing the main theorem by applying Kato's pushforward homomorphism $\pi_*:QK_T(G/B)\to QK_T(G/P)$ in equivariant quantum $K$-theory \cite{Kato2}.)

