\label{simon}
    Let $(\rho_0, u_0) $ be some initial data such that $u_0 \in H^1_0(\Omega) \cap H^s(\Omega)$, $\operatorname{div} u_0 = 0$ in $\Omega$ and $\rho_0 \in L^\infty(\Omega)$, with $\overline{C} \geqslant \rho_0 \geqslant \underline{C}>0$ for some constants $\overline{C}, \underline{C}$.
    Then there exists $T>0$ and a (unique) solution $(\rho,u, \Pi)$ of \eqref{limitsys} such taht $0<\underline{C} \leqslant \rho \leqslant \overline{C}$ that satisfy
