\begin{definition}[(coherence)]\label{rec:coherence}
	Let $ \Xcal $ be \atopos.
	We say that $\Xcal $ is \defn{$ 0 $-coherent} (or \defn{quasicompact}) if for every effective epimorphism $ e \colon \coprod_{i \in I} U_i \surjection 1_{\Xcal} $, there exists a finite subset $ I_0 \subset I $ such that the restriction $ \coprod_{i \in I_0} U_i \surjection 1_{\Xcal} $ of $ e $ is still an effective epimorphism.
	Let $ n \geq 0 $, and define $n$-coherence of \topoi and their objects recursively as follows.
	\begin{enumerate}
