\end{theorem}." Instead, to prove the main theorem, we use the spectral gap of the elliptic Kodaira-Spencer Laplacians, namely:
\begin{theorem}\label{theorem spectral gap kodaira spencer laplacians}
Let $(M,g)$ be a complete K\"ahler manifold. If $\Delta_{\delbar,sw}$ has a spectral gap in $L^2\Lambda^{p,q}$, then for $b\in\{s,w\}$ the operators $\tilde\Delta_{A,sb}$ and $\tilde\Delta_{BC,bw}$ have a spectral gap in $L^2\Lambda^{p,q}$.
\end{theorem}
We also establish a spectral gap for the Varouchas Laplacians:
\begin{theorem}\label{theorem spectral gap varouchas laplacians}
    Let $(M,g)$ be a complete K\"ahler manifold. 
    If $\Delta_{\delbar,sw}$ has a spectral gap in $L^2\Lambda^{p,q}$, $L^2\Lambda^{p-1,q}$ and $L^2\Lambda^{p,q-1}$, then $\square_{A,sw}$ has a spectral gap in $L^2\Lambda^{p,q}$. If $\Delta_{\delbar,sw}$ has a spectral gap in $L^2\Lambda^{p,q}$, $L^2\Lambda^{p+1,q}$ and $L^2\Lambda^{p,q+1}$, then $\square_{BC,sw}$ has a spectral gap in $L^2\Lambda^{p,q}$.
