Finally, it notes the role of the spectral gap hypothesis: without it, "the images of the closed extensions of $d$, $\partial$, $\delbar$, and $\partial\delbar$ fail to be closed," so the assumption is "essential" for a direct $L^2$ analogue of the classical $\partial\delbar$-Lemma.

