for $s_{i} \not = s'_{i}$, \\
with arbitrary $a, b, x$ defined by the spectrum.
\end{thm}
\begin{proof}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item First, we prove that these sets of matrices are $T$-invariant. For case~\ref{first} we can use a system~\ref{eq}. Considering $a=d$, $b = -c$ we get

\begingroup\centering
    \begin{equation*}
    \begin{cases}
