\begin{theorem}\cite[Proposition 6.2]{Coulson_2017}\label{Thm2}
For any nonnegative integer $J$ and $1\leq i\leq r$, we have
\begin{align}\label{ll1}
\mathcal{C}_{(r-1)J+\ell}(q)=\mathcal{E}_{r,i,J}(q),
\end{align}
where $\ell=r-i+1$.
\end{theorem}
gives the G\"ollnitz-Gordon-Andrews identities; hence the main theorem is a direct corollary of this theorem.” It then outlines the proof strategy for proving the general identities
\begin{align}\label{ll1}
